From 49dca8661e8f44567a3b4fe429f250fe1fddadae Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 17:40:16 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ci: pin every action, so the workflow can start at all

The first run after activation failed in seven seconds, before any step:

  The actions actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-node@v4, and
  actions/upload-artifact@v4 are not allowed in voxgig/create-system
  because all actions must be pinned to a full-length commit SHA.

This repository requires SHA pinning and GitHub enforces it at workflow
load. The floating tags ci.yml carried while it was dormant were therefore
not the cosmetic difference from docs.yml and publish.yml that the
activation commit called them: they were the reason the workflow could not
run. Recording that plainly, because nothing runnable locally catches it --
the npm steps were verified and passed, and could never have exposed a
policy applied before they execute.

checkout and setup-node reuse the exact pins docs.yml and publish.yml
already run, so those are this repository's own trusted choices rather than
new ones, and it upgrades both from the v4 majors the dormant file named.
upload-artifact has no precedent here, so it is pinned to the commit its
`v4` tag names -- the version the file already declared, pinned rather than
upgraded, resolved from the action's own repository.

ci/README.md replaces its "actions are not pinned here" note with why they
must be, quoting the failure, so the next person adding an action knows a
SHA is required before it will start.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01RBcWm7ygX2tNhUtqtTJbAh
---
 .github/workflows/ci.yml | 24 +++++++++++++++++++++---
 ci/README.md             | 26 ++++++++++++++++++--------
 2 files changed, 39 insertions(+), 11 deletions(-)

diff --git a/.github/workflows/ci.yml b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
index 8681cb0..64d14d0 100644
--- a/.github/workflows/ci.yml
+++ b/.github/workflows/ci.yml
@@ -6,6 +6,24 @@
 # move are in ci/README.md: what a coverage gate would have to account for,
 # and the one check this workflow still does not make.
 #
+# EVERY ACTION IS PINNED TO A FULL-LENGTH COMMIT SHA, because this repository
+# requires it and GitHub enforces that before a single step runs. The first
+# run after activation failed in seven seconds on exactly that:
+#
+#   The actions actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-node@v4, and
+#   actions/upload-artifact@v4 are not allowed in voxgig/create-system
+#   because all actions must be pinned to a full-length commit SHA.
+#
+# So the floating tags this file carried while dormant were never a style
+# nit; they were why it could not start. Nothing runnable locally catches
+# this -- the policy is applied at workflow load, not by npm.
+#
+# checkout and setup-node reuse the exact pins docs.yml and publish.yml
+# already run, so they are this repository's own trusted choice rather than
+# a new one. upload-artifact has no precedent here, so it is pinned to the
+# commit its `v4` tag names -- the version this file already declared,
+# pinned rather than upgraded.
+#
 # COVERAGE IS REPORTED, NOT GATED, and ci/README.md says why a threshold set
 # from the headline figure would lock in an illusion: Node reports only the
 # files a test loaded, so dist/create.js is missing from the table rather
@@ -27,11 +45,11 @@ jobs:
   test:
     runs-on: ubuntu-latest
     steps:
-      - uses: actions/checkout@v4
+      - uses: actions/checkout@3d3c42e5aac5ba805825da76410c181273ba90b1 # v7
 
       # package.json declares engines.node >= 20; 22 is what the generated
       # projects deploy on, so build against the same.
-      - uses: actions/setup-node@v4
+      - uses: actions/setup-node@820762786026740c76f36085b0efc47a31fe5020 # v7
         with:
           node-version: '22'
           cache: npm
@@ -52,7 +70,7 @@ jobs:
 
       - name: upload coverage
         if: always()
-        uses: actions/upload-artifact@v4
+        uses: actions/upload-artifact@ea165f8d65b6e75b540449e92b4886f43607fa02 # v4
         with:
           name: coverage
           path: coverage.lcov
diff --git a/ci/README.md b/ci/README.md
index fc0d08f..4b2bd48 100644
--- a/ci/README.md
+++ b/ci/README.md
@@ -39,11 +39,21 @@ Worth adding as a job once they are released. It is the check that would
 have caught the pins being wrong in the first place: `@voxgig/build` was
 pinned to 4.10.0, a version that never existed on npm.
 
-## Actions are not pinned here
-
-`ci.yml` uses floating major tags (`actions/checkout@v4`,
-`actions/setup-node@v4`, `actions/upload-artifact@v4`), while `docs.yml`
-and `publish.yml` pin every action to a full-length commit SHA. That
-difference is not deliberate — it is what the file carried while it was
-dormant and nothing ran it. Pinning it to match the sibling workflows is
-worth doing; the majors are behind those files too, which use v7.
+## Actions must be pinned, and the repository enforces it
+
+Every action in `ci.yml` is pinned to a full-length commit SHA. This is not
+a style preference: the repository requires it and GitHub checks it before
+a single step runs. The first run after activation failed in seven seconds,
+having reached no step at all:
+
+```
+The actions actions/checkout@v4, actions/setup-node@v4, and
+actions/upload-artifact@v4 are not allowed in voxgig/create-system
+because all actions must be pinned to a full-length commit SHA.
+```
+
+The floating tags this file carried while dormant were therefore never a
+cosmetic difference from `docs.yml` and `publish.yml` — they were why it
+could not start. Nothing runnable locally catches this, because the policy
+is applied when the workflow loads rather than by anything `npm` does. A
+change that adds an action here needs its SHA before it will run at all.
